  "summary": "350 engine cars with air conditioning (C60): A/C compressor mounting brackets. The compressor hangs on a front bracket [3] and a rear bracket [12], which bolt to a front support [8] and a rear support [14] on the engine; shims [11] go between the rear bracket and compressor as needed, set by a mandatory assembly sequence. The rear support (View A) is held by bolt [15] and a nut [10] on stud [13]; the front support by bolts [7] plus engine-supplied bolts.",
